Z||000000||BOILERMAKER||04-07-2000||09:35 AM||||I neeed help on a pin-out for connector C203.  The engine is a V6 for a GT and I am finding that the J pin on the C203 connector doesn't have a wire.  Before I put the engine in I need to know what this goes to and what it does.  I haven't been able to find it in the Haynes or Service manuals, but only had a small amount of time to look this morning.||||reg||1
Z||000001||80's BOY||04-07-2000||03:05 PM||||dude, i had this same problem but i had 3 wires out from 3 pins. you can only find this info in a factory Fiero service manual. if you describe the wire color and position to me, i might be able to help you. if not, then pull apart your connector and dig through all the black, sticky connector grease. see if you can match a piece of the wire to one of the holes from the backside of the connector. these pull out from the backside only with needlenosed pliers. good luck!!||||reg||12
